  "description": "<p>After some discussion in the Hydra community &#8211; <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/topic/hydra-tech/2P2CCrk4LaU/discussion\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://groups.google.com/d/topic/hydra-tech/2P2CCrk4LaU/discussion</a> &#8211; we're thinking this new state might be used as an initial state in deposit workflows where mediation must occur to \"publish\" an object, or could also possibly be used to \"withdraw\" an object without deleting it or marking it for deletion. This also achieves parity with the three object states provided by Fedora 3.</p>",
